            <ArticleTitle>A coronary teaching program in a community hospital.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In conclusion, the teaching program we developed appears to meet the needs originally established by the audit. Nurses are provided with a method of assessment, evaluation, and documentation. The program also provides a means of teaching continuity while following a structured time schedule that allows for recognition and satisfaction of individual patient needs. The patient teaching record provides the final tool as a reference and ongoing source of evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
